      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your seminar, start by clearly defining the classic social contract premise of ceded individual liberty for state protection. Next, analyze how modern surveillance technologies test this balance, juxtaposing security gains against privacy erosion. Conclude by presenting two main arguments: either surveillance fundamentally breaches the implicit trust, or it represents a necessary, yet precarious, evolution of the social contract to meet new threats. This structure allows you to explore the tension rather than just picking a side.",
